Actually, let me look at what happens after `mbedtls_x509_crt_free(crt)` is called inside `x509_crt_parse_der_core`. After it returns an error, the caller `mbedtls_x509_crt_parse_der_internal` at line 1351-1357:
```c
if( ( ret = x509_crt_parse_der_core( crt, buf, buflen, make_copy ) ) != 0 )
{
    if( prev )
        prev->next = NULL;

    if( crt != chain )
        mbedtls_free( crt );

    return( ret );
}
```

So `mbedtls_free(crt)` frees the certificate structure itself. But `mbedtls_x509_crt_free` already handled all the internal cleanup. That seems fine.

